<title>JAPAN: No big impact on Japan banks from Thai turmoil-MOF.</title>
<headline>No big impact on Japan banks from Thai turmoil-MOF.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-07-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Japan's Ministry of Finance (MOF) has not heard of any specific cases where a Japanese financial institution has been seriously affected by the currency turmoil in Thailand, a ministry official told reporters on Friday.</p>
<p>Asked if any financial institution has been seriously affected by economic instability in Thailand, the official said: &quot;So far...no particular institution has been so seriously affected.&quot;</p>
<p>But he added that any kind of currency fluctuation would have some impact on domestic as well as foreign institutions.</p>
</text>
